WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:09.190
Speaker 1: Speaking of good signs, a very
bad situation for an Alaska state senator

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:14.959
is that Alaska Airlines has banned her from
flying on Alaska Airlines.

00:00:14.959 --> 00:00:18.770
I'm talking here about State Senator Laura
Reinbold.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:25.010
Tim Thompson, spokesman for Alaska Airlines,
told the Anchorage Daily News over the weekend,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:29.820
quote, We have notified Senator Laura Reinbold
that she is not permitted to fly with us for

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:36.550
her continued refusal to comply with employee
instruction regarding the current mask policy.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.980
Apparently, she has not only been refusing
to wear a mask, she was even recorded arguing

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.530
at Juneau International Airport, arguing with
an Alaska Airlines staff member about mask

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:48.960
policy.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.470
And the video appears to show airline staff
telling her the mask must be on.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.430
It must cover your mouth.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:02.750
It must also cover your nose like the basics,
we're going back to March 20 20 unmasking

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:09.130
and she had been apparently asking about a
mask exemption with upright employees, with

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.700
uptight employees at the counter.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.610
She said I was reasonable with all Alaska
Airlines employees and that she did ultimately

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:17.610
board the flight.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.409
But she's been vocally opposed to any covid-19
mitigation measures.

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:25.380
She has objected to the Alaska Airlines mask
policy that was enacted before the federal

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.060
government enacted a mask policy.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.140
Alaska Airlines had already been saying even
before Biden came in.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.780
You have to wear a mask.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.380
She's been calling Alaska Airlines staff mask
bullies.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:42.189
And when she was asked by flight attendants
when boarding the flight to put the mask on,

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:47.909
I guess she went nuts and then has sent some
kind of apology to the staff.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:50.659
It's all completely crazy.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:56.500
And this is the only airline she can take
to go from between Anchorage and Juneau unless

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.939
she starts flying private or like, could she
connect somewhere in the mainland?

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:05.900
Imagine having to fly from Juneau to like
Seattle and then Seattle to Anchorage because

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.090
she's banned.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.959
Actually, even that flight, I think, is only
in Alaska.

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:14.500
And I don't know what the hell she's going
to do, quite frankly, because if you're an

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:19.440
Alaska state senator needing to regularly
get back and forth to Anchorage, there aren't

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.150
really other options other than Alaska Airlines.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:27.160
And, you know, I know a lot of people in the
audience have dealt with the mass stuff when

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.420
flying, but you don't necessarily expect it
from a sitting state senator.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.340
Even on my flight, I talked about this on
my I flew a different not Alaska Airlines,

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.890
which as far as I know, Alaska Airlines is
being really good on the mask stuff.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.250
Not every airline is.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:47.350
I flew a different airline to Aruba last month,
fully vaccinated, of course, and with a mask

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.830
and everything.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:52.250
And there was absolutely no enforcement of
masking.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:57.989
There were a lot of people sitting near me
who were playing sort of coy with the food

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:03.860
and drink policy, where even though the airline
announced multiple times, if you were actively

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:07.200
eating or drinking, you can take your mask
off.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.780
If you are between sips or bites, put the
mask on.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.430
And there were a bunch of people on the plane
who were doing the thing where they take the

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:19.070
mask off and they hold their drink up.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:25.260
So they appear to be in the process of actively
drinking and then they just watch a two hour

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.200
movie on the TV screen and just hold the drink.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.010
There was no enforcement whatsoever.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:34.739
At one point I saw a woman get up from her
seat and go to the bathroom, walk by flight

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:39.410
attendants with just no mask, and then walk
back to her seat.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:44.370
And I'd say half of the people near me, the
mask wasn't even covering the nose.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:48.780
And, you know, as I said, I wouldn't have
traveled if I weren't vaccinated.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:54.530
So I wasn't bothered in that I was, you know,
hiding, thinking I'm going to get sick.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:58.640
You needed a negative to everybody on the
plane, needed a negative test in order to

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.640
board.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.989
And I was vaccinated.

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:02.720
It wasn't because of that.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.370
But if the rules are right now to fly, you
wear the mask.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.370
I'm going to play the game.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.330
If I don't want to wear the mask on the plane,
I'll just say I'm not going to travel for

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.150
the time being because I wanted to travel.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.230
I wore the mask.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.349
Whatever I think about my personal level of
risk, that I think is what's frustrating,

00:04:17.349 --> 00:04:22.159
which is, you know, the rules when you get
on, you're told when you book the flight,

00:04:22.159 --> 00:04:25.979
you're told when you check in for the flight,
you're not even allowed near the gate without

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:28.779
a mask, you're told, via announcements.

00:04:28.779 --> 00:04:33.490
And then for Laura Reinbold to just continue
arguing about this, you don't have to fly.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.749
Now, you might say, well, she does have to
fly.

00:04:35.749 --> 00:04:38.779
She has to get back and forth from Anchorage
to Juneau because she's a state senator.

00:04:38.779 --> 00:04:39.849
Well, OK.

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:41.069
She could look at driving.

00:04:41.069 --> 00:04:42.159
She could look at chartering a plane.

00:04:42.159 --> 00:04:46.279
She doesn't have to fly on Alaska Airlines,
nor does she have a right to fly on Alaska

00:04:46.279 --> 00:04:47.550
Airlines.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.249
And she is now banned from Alaska Airlines.

00:04:50.249 --> 00:04:54.939
No word on how she will commute for her work
as an Alaska state senator.

00:04:54.939 --> 00:04:57.059
It's not going to be that much longer, guys.

00:04:57.059 --> 00:04:58.489
If you're supposed to wear the mask, just
wear the mask.

